{
  "id": "UP050",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Transurethral resection of the prostate (TURP)",
  "description": "A transurethral resection of the prostate (TURP) removes obstructing prostate tissue causing urinary problems. During this outpatient or brief overnight inpatient procedure, your urologist passes a resectoscope through the urethra to the prostate and uses radiofrequency energy to vaporize obstructive tissue. The procedure takes 30-90 minutes. Most people experience dramatically improved urinary stream within weeks. You may have temporary blood-tinged urine and mild discomfort for a few days. Activity restrictions last 3-4 weeks. Long-term success rates are excellent with symptom improvement lasting many years. This type of procedure can be performed various ways, including initial / revision, and the cost may vary depending on the specific approach or service provided.",
